# Linux system packages, one per line. The Linux counterpart to Brewfile.
#
# Read by bin/install.sh (see read_pacfile). Blank lines and everything after
# a `#` are ignored, so group entries under comments however you like.
#
# Only list what you actually want on a machine. Omarchy already provides the
# kernel, boot chain, PipeWire/Wayland plumbing, Hyprland core and the
# omarchy-* framework packages, so those are deliberately left out here.
#
# Any entry that is not in an enabled sync database is treated as AUR-only and
# routed to yay automatically, since pacman resolves its whole batch up front
# and aborts everything on a single name it cannot find. The split depends only
# on your repositories, not on what happens to be installed already, so a fresh
# machine and an existing one take the same path.
#
# Deliberately excluded: linux, linux-firmware, mkinitcpio, limine,
# efibootmgr, sof-firmware, intel-ucode, wireless-regdb, kernel-modules-hook,
# btrfs-progs, dosfstools, exfatprogs, zram-generator, pipewire*, wireplapper,
# libpulse, vulkan-intel, vpl-gpu-rt, intel-media-driver, quickshell, hyprland,
# hyprland-guiutils, asdcontrol, uwsm, xdg-terminal-exec, pamixer, sddm,
# fprintd, libfprint, gnome-keyring, networkmanager, bluez*, xdg-desktop-portal-*,
# nss-mdns, base, pacman-contrib, elsewhen.

